# The app's own Genius API client token, baked into release builds.
# Register the client at https://genius.com/api-clients and copy the
# "Client Access Token" here, then build: npm run build
#
# This is NOT a secret once shipped - it sits in the main bundle and anyone
# can unpack it. Every install shares its rate limit, so keep a client that
# is only used for this, and expect to rotate it if it is ever revoked.
# Leave it unset and lyrics simply ask the person for a token of their own.
GENIUS_TOKEN=

# WARNING about names: electron-vite inlines any variable prefixed VITE_,
# MAIN_VITE_, PRELOAD_VITE_ or RENDERER_VITE_ straight into the bundles,
# automatically, whether or not electron.vite.config.ts mentions it in its
# `define` block. A secret given one of those prefixes ships to everyone
# with no diff anywhere to notice it. Never prefix a secret that way.
